### Skills vs scripts

`scripts/` is the operational toolkit (Python, git-tracked,
runnable end-to-end). `skills/` is for things with a `SKILL.md` +
recurring workflow + the right shape for `skills.read()`. Decide
case-by-case and don't duplicate shared infra skills — those live in
the harness's own `skills/` directory.

For recurring work, use the `create_timer` skill (it ships in the
harness's `skills/create_timer/`). It generates a `systemd --user`
timer + service pair that POSTs to the harness's
`/api/v1/internal/timer` endpoint with a prompt.

